  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">MIV kvalitetss&#xe4;kring st&#xf6;d till DGMM</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SMA quality assurance support to DGMM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet syftar till att fr&#xe4;mja ett r&#xe4;ttighetsbaserat system f&#xf6;r internationellt skydd av flyktingar. Migrationsverket kommer att st&#xf6;dja DGMM: (1) i att introducera ett kvalitetss&#xe4;kringssystem f&#xf6;r att best&#xe4;mma flyktingars status utif&#xe5;n ett vedertaget uniformt system; (2) i att bli en mer f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;gbar och transparent organsiation; samt, (3) i att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla att utsatta asyls&#xf6;kande och migranters r&#xe4;ttigheter skyddas, s&#xe4;rskilt n&#xe4;r det g&#xe4;ller kvinnor och flickor, minder&#xe5;riga, samt HBTQ-personer. Migrationsverket kommer att st&#xf6;dja institutionell kapacitet och standard inom DGMM, s&#xe5; att de p&#xe5; ett adekvat s&#xe4;tt kan planera migrationshanteringen och samtidigt s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla effektiva och r&#xe4;ttvisa hanteringsprocedurer.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Swedish Migration Agency has applied to Sida for funding of 7 000 000 SEK to carry out the project entitled &quot;SMA Quality Assurance Support to DGMM&quot; during the period 2017-2020. 
The project aims supports the DGMM to promote a rights-based approach to international protection. The SMA will assist the DGMM to: (1) introduce a refugee status determination quality assurance system that promotes uniform and correct decisions; (2) operate in a more transparent, predictable and credible manner, and; (3) protect the rights of vulnerable asylum-seekers and migrants with specific needs, specifically as concerns women and girls, minors, and LGBTI+ persons. The Swedish Migration Agency (SMA), will support the DGMM in the creation of the institutional means and standards that will enable it to adequately plan their migration management policy and ensure efficient and fair procedures for migrants..
The intervention&apos;s total budget is 7 000 000 SEK.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The impact goal is for Turkey to discharge fully of its international obligations under international and regional human rights and refugee law insofar as concerns applicants for international protection.</narrative>
  </description>
